{title: 052 - Now the Day Is Over}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #052 • MERRIAL • 6.5.7.5}
{lyricist: Sabine Baring-Gould}
{composer: Joseph Barnby}
{key: A}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 52}
{meta: tune MERRIAL}
{meta: meter 6.5.7.5}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Now the [C#m/G#]day [E7/G#]is over,
[D/A]night is [C#/G#]drawing [D/A]nigh,
[D#dim]Shadows [Bm]of [E/B]the [D/A]evening
[A]steal [C#m/G#]across the [A]sky.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]Father, [C#m/G#]give [E7/G#]the weary,
[D/A]calm and [C#/G#]sweet [Bm]repose;
[D#dim]With Thy [Bm]tenderest [C#m/G#]blessing
[A]May [C#m/G#]our [F#7]eyelids [A]close.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]Through the [C#m/G#]long [E7/G#]night watches,
[D/A]may thine [C#/G#]angels [D/A]spread
[D#dim]Their [Bm]white [E/B]wings [D/A]above [A]me,
[A]watching [F#7]round [C#m/G#]my [A]bed.
{end_of_verse}
